    not_duplicate_of: []  # d2a3
    pr_ref:  # d2a3
    description: "Residual of WI-hasul (grants for the 15 C headers that declare NO I/O; docs/surveys/c-stdlib-module-io-enumeration.md). The core I/O headers cannot be granted complete: each declares I/O c.yaml does not row. Probed from glibc (gcc -E) and checked against c.yaml on 2026-09-30, unrowed I/O includes: stdio popen/pclose (subprocess), perror/puts/vprintf/vfprintf/vdprintf/dprintf (logging), freopen/fdopen, fseeko/ftello/fgetpos/fsetpos, renameat, tmpnam/tempnam; unistd pread/pwrite, pipe, dup/dup2, lseek, unlinkat/linkat/symlinkat/readlinkat, fsync, fchown/lchown, getlogin (host_info_read), sethostname; stdlib setenv/unsetenv/putenv (env_write), secure_getenv (env_read), mkdtemp/mktemp, realpath, getloadavg; sys/socket socket/socketpair/bind/listen/accept4/shutdown/getsockopt/setsockopt/getsockname/getpeername; sys/stat mkfifo/mknod/fchmod/fchmodat/utimensat/futimens/umask; fcntl fcntl/posix_fallocate; dirent fdopendir/readdir_r. Each row needs its boundary (and mode/ambiguous_names care: C has no namespaces), measured A/B (recall), and then a per-header completeness audit in the survey. On measurement 0023's cohort these headers are the main remaining blockers besides linux/* and net* headers and first-party headers (filed separately)."  # d2a3
    fields: {}  # d2a3
- op: discuss  # ee7f
  at: '2026-10-03T17:38:20Z'  # ee7f
  by: agent  # ee7f
