  clock: 2  # ee7f
  nonce: ee7f  # ee7f
  message: "A CAUTION FOR THIS ITEM'S ROW ADDITIONS, from WI-vafad tranche 3 (2026-10-03, docs/audits/0022 T3-A1). The sweep ACCEPTED removing c `stdio.{fseek, ftell, rewind, ungetc}` from fs_read (WI-paful-rudar-lijof-sopog-dujuf-bokik-lajob-dihaj). They move or report a stream position, or push back into the buffer, and read no data. rust.yaml:70 and :186 and python.yaml:2062 deliberately leave seek / tell unrowed. This item's list includes fseeko / ftello / fgetpos / fsetpos and unistd lseek. Rowing them under fs_read by analogy with today's fseek row would extend the shape that sweep found wrong. Suggest leaving them unrowed (or naming them in the completeness audit as position calls that cross nothing) unless the fseek item resolves the other way."  # ee7f
